    "title": "In the AI Era, the Most Valuable Things Are Not Big Ideas, but Weird Little Thoughts",
    "summary": "AI lowers the cost of testing small products, giving strange little ideas like digital rituals, overthinking translators, and interactive stories a chance to become real products.",
